    1 &\geq 4y(i)(1-y(i)).
\end{align*}
The last inequality follows because its right hand side is maximized for $y(i)=\frac{1}{2}$. This maximal value is equal to one and our claim follows.
It follows that $u_2(i) \geq u_1(i)=\log(t(i)/x(i))$ because
\begin{equation*}
