If there is a crossing, then because the transmission has to be correct due to Proposition~\ref{prop::trivial stuff}.\ref{it::cross implies correct transmission}. In that case the true segment is enlarged by Proposition~\ref{prop::trivial stuff}.\ref{it::correct transmission increases true segment}  and the first statement follows.
For the second statement we first consider the case that $T(i-1)$ is not central. Then it is clear that
\begin{equation*}
